WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.510
February 2014.

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.410
Across the Somerset Levels,
farmland lies under water.

3
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:09.510
Some villages can only be reached by boat.

4
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.650
The flooding began in mid-December
2013, and lasted into spring.

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:20.450
About 100 million cubic metres of
water covered 65 square kilometres.

6
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:25.210
Over 200 homes were cut off,
some for more than two months.

7
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.970
So why did the water stay for so long?

8
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.310
In this mission, you'll map the Levels,
and sort the floods' physical and human

9
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.550
causes.

10
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.130
Then you'll weigh what
the floods did to people,

11
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.230
farms and wildlife.

12
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:43.390
Your mission: find out why the water
stayed on the Somerset Levels for so long.
